Align the basicobjects sub-library version with the packaged 0.2.0 release.

The ding-libs 0.6.2 distribution is the last upstream release that still
ships libbasicobjects as a standalone library (sub-library version 0.1.1
in version.m4 and the pre-generated configure script).  The OHPCD task
catalogue requests this library as 0.2.0, and the Conan recipe version
must match.  Keep both version sources consistent so that the installed
basicobjects.pc reports the same version as the Conan reference, both for
the pre-generated configure (used with the official release tarball) and
for the autoreconf path (codeload tag archive fallback, which reads
version.m4).

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -12683,7 +12683,7 @@

 REF_ARRAY_VERSION=0.1.5

-BASICOBJECTS_VERSION=0.1.1
+BASICOBJECTS_VERSION=0.2.0

 INI_CONFIG_VERSION=1.3.1

--- a/version.m4
+++ b/version.m4
@@ -14,5 +14,5 @@
 m4_define([DHASH_VERSION_NUMBER], [0.5.0])
 m4_define([COLLECTION_VERSION_NUMBER], [0.7.0])
 m4_define([REF_ARRAY_VERSION_NUMBER], [0.1.5])
-m4_define([BASICOBJECTS_VERSION_NUMBER], [0.1.1])
+m4_define([BASICOBJECTS_VERSION_NUMBER], [0.2.0])
 m4_define([INI_CONFIG_VERSION_NUMBER], [1.3.1])
